00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.740
These are our spaceships, the Speebs.

00:13:38.740 --> 00:13:41.740
Were they built in accordance with our original design?

00:13:41.740 --> 00:13:43.310
Why, yes, exactly.

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:45.640
Why, do you find something wrong?

00:13:45.640 --> 00:13:48.050
No, I think they're wonderful.

00:13:48.050 --> 00:13:50.150
I have to confess, I am quite surprised.

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:52.300
I didn't think you could build them so quickly.

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:54.040
Well, we didn't do it alone.

00:13:54.040 --> 00:13:55.920
All the nations in the world did it.

00:13:55.920 --> 00:13:57.740
Well, it's marvelous all the same.

00:13:57.740 --> 00:13:59.120
Congratulations, Doctor.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:00.000
Shall we move on now?

00:14:00.000 --> 00:14:03.190
- Congratulations. - This way, gentlemen, this way.

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:18.150
We're mainly concerned with adjusting the instruments and controls inside the ships.

00:14:18.150 --> 00:14:20.470
Actual firing is just a question of time now.

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:25.730
What is the deviation on the wave motion index?

00:14:25.730 --> 00:14:29.920
Well, here. I was just checking the figures on that, Professor.

00:14:30.670 --> 00:14:35.220
It's 1 to 100,000 in the atmosphere and 1 to 1 million in outer space.

