01:13:02.460 --> 01:13:05.960
An explosion accompanied the return of the surviving spaceship to the Earth.

01:13:05.960 --> 01:13:08.780
An explosion that was to rock the course of humanity

01:13:08.780 --> 01:13:14.280
and change the entire Earth into a fighting organism with but one single point of view.

01:13:14.280 --> 01:13:20.190
All over the world, people of all nations locked together to seek safety in a common union.

01:13:20.190 --> 01:13:25.140
They insisted that their leaders should all work together against this common enemy

01:13:25.140 --> 01:13:27.140
and for the defense of the Earth.

01:13:27.140 --> 01:13:30.000
From country to country, the cry was taken up.

01:13:30.320 --> 01:13:35.560
And it echoed across the surface of the earth until it was heard in the halls of the United Nations.

01:13:35.840 --> 01:13:45.240
We must check, by every means at our disposal, the barbarous ambitions of the Natal spacemen.

01:13:47.080 --> 01:13:52.640
They are bound to fall upon us with renewed attack after reinforcing their base.

01:13:53.550 --> 01:13:58.740
Doctor, can you estimate how big a leap they have over us in their space technique?

01:13:59.680 --> 01:14:00.000
Were there...

01:14:00.000 --> 01:14:05.770
is quite advanced when compared to ours, at least from the time viewpoint. While

01:14:05.770 --> 01:14:09.810
their theoretical knowledge may not be very far ahead of ours, it is clear that

01:14:09.810 --> 01:14:14.360
we should be ready to resist their attack in the best way we can. I suggest

01:14:14.360 --> 01:14:18.640
that the small scouting craft we now have undergoing trials should be armed

01:14:18.640 --> 01:14:22.200
and converted into fighter ships to intercept the attacking saucers outside

01:14:22.200 --> 01:14:30.000
our atmosphere. Gentlemen, we are at war with the planet Natal. I'm sure each and every one of us

01:14:30.730 --> 01:14:33.170
that diplomatic procedures can be bypassed

01:14:33.170 --> 01:14:35.930
in the present emergency, and we should mobilize.

01:14:40.140 --> 01:14:42.700
An emergency order for the construction of fighter rockets

01:14:42.700 --> 01:14:45.500
was issued to all advanced factories throughout the world.

01:14:45.820 --> 01:14:47.600
Day and night, men and machines struggled

01:14:47.600 --> 01:14:49.920
to complete production schedules in time.

01:14:50.260 --> 01:14:52.260
The fate of the world hung in the balance.

01:15:01.180 --> 01:15:05.300
On the cold Siberian plains, fighter rocket bases mushroomed into growth

01:15:05.300 --> 01:15:09.240
to be followed quickly by similar launching sites on the plains of Texas

01:15:09.240 --> 01:15:11.840
and at the Science Center base in Japan.

01:15:36.460 --> 01:15:39.460
Unidentified object approaching from fourth sector, range 8,000 miles.

01:15:40.340 --> 01:15:43.230
Then we'll put him right about here. Stay with him, on red alert.

01:15:43.470 --> 01:15:45.930
Yes, sir. Red alert. Check on Siberia.

01:15:46.420 --> 01:15:47.260
Siberia here.

01:15:47.580 --> 01:15:48.540
And Texas, is it ready?

01:15:48.800 --> 01:15:49.640
Ready in Texas.

01:15:49.960 --> 01:15:50.500
Ready in Tokyo?

01:15:50.500 --> 01:15:50.900
Ready in Tokyo.

01:16:04.350 --> 01:16:04.870
Thank you.

01:16:47.280 --> 01:16:49.990
- This is space control calling Russia over.

01:16:49.990 --> 01:16:51.360
- Emmelman speaking.

01:16:51.360 --> 01:16:54.610
My first fighter squadron is now taking off.

01:17:01.120 --> 01:17:04.000
We've done our best, Professor. There really isn't much more to say.

01:17:05.570 --> 01:17:08.570
It better work the first time. We won't be able to send anyone else out.

01:17:09.330 --> 01:17:10.050
That's so.

01:17:46.190 --> 01:17:48.520
Rocket 1, come in please, over.

01:17:48.520 --> 01:17:51.640
Closing in East Sector, objects approaching on course.

01:17:51.640 --> 01:17:53.410
Looks like it might be the enemy.

01:17:53.410 --> 01:17:57.720
We're moving in to investigate.

01:18:05.880 --> 01:18:07.140
force of enemy saucers.

01:18:07.520 --> 01:18:09.760
They are escorting a mother ship with space torpedoes.

01:18:10.190 --> 01:18:11.590
We are going in after them.

01:18:11.990 --> 01:18:12.770
An all-out offensive.

01:18:17.030 --> 01:18:17.930
Attention, emergency.

01:18:19.380 --> 01:18:20.760
Enemy forces are approaching.

01:18:22.380 --> 01:18:25.670
All defense units, report to East Sector to repel invaders.

01:18:27.170 --> 01:18:30.000
Four, three, two.

01:18:30.700 --> 01:18:32.280
- One. - Zero.

01:19:05.470 --> 01:19:07.290
Group B, altitude 4,000 kilometers.

01:19:07.760 --> 01:19:09.200
We'll rendezvous in 30 seconds.

01:19:16.330 --> 01:19:19.980
Captain of the reinforcement group, altitude 5,000 kilometers.

01:19:20.430 --> 01:19:22.860
I have the enemy in sight and am preparing to attack.

01:19:23.140 --> 01:19:23.580
That is all.

01:19:52.910 --> 01:19:53.520
Get them.

01:21:44.940 --> 01:21:46.480
They fired a space torpedo at Earth.

01:22:04.060 --> 01:22:06.200
Space Torpedoes Approaching Earth!

01:22:06.200 --> 01:22:08.310
Space Torpedoes Approaching Earth!

01:22:08.310 --> 01:22:12.810
You must leave your sector and go after them

01:22:12.810 --> 01:22:14.760
and destroy the torpedoes.

01:22:14.760 --> 01:22:15.620
Right.

01:22:15.620 --> 01:22:22.280
The mother ship has gotten through.

01:22:22.280 --> 01:22:23.320
Escorted by six saucers.

01:22:23.320 --> 01:22:24.560
Get them.

01:22:24.560 --> 01:22:27.320
You have them on the space radar?

01:22:27.320 --> 01:22:30.000
Yes, sir. They're inside.

01:22:30.000 --> 01:22:33.460
Second sector, on a gradual approach, we will track.

01:22:33.500 --> 01:22:35.670
- Don't let him get away. - We will hold him, sir.

01:24:08.220 --> 01:24:11.260
Mothership is approaching Tokyo with escort!

01:24:11.260 --> 01:24:14.340
Mothership is approaching Tokyo with escort!

01:26:20.540 --> 01:26:23.560
A reporting, we have destroyed the bulk of the enemy fleet

01:26:23.560 --> 01:26:26.730
with two exceptions, the mother ship and one saucer.

01:26:26.730 --> 01:26:30.000
- Keep out of the way then, we'll take over now.

01:26:30.870 --> 01:26:34.150
Thirty degrees north of the space terminal and seven miles high.

01:26:39.020 --> 01:26:44.190
Beacon ready.

01:26:45.310 --> 01:26:45.710
Danby.

01:26:47.200 --> 01:26:47.480
Fire.

01:26:47.900 --> 01:26:48.220
Fire.

01:26:51.270 --> 01:26:54.510
This is Group A reporting.

01:26:55.260 --> 01:26:58.200
We are very low on fuel and we must return to base.

01:26:58.820 --> 01:27:00.000
It's up to you now.

01:27:00.640 --> 01:27:03.840
The enemy saucer and mothership are nearing your position.

01:27:04.600 --> 01:27:07.390
- Over. - Well done.

01:27:07.960 --> 01:27:08.660
Group A.

01:27:18.640 --> 01:27:19.740
- Prepare to fire. - Ready.

01:27:20.250 --> 01:27:28.980
- Answer. - Three-two.

01:27:29.080 --> 01:27:29.730
Two ready.

01:27:31.660 --> 01:27:32.470
Fire!

01:28:40.170 --> 01:28:42.290
Here's a report from space radar search, commander.

01:28:43.020 --> 01:28:45.000
No indication of further enemy activity.

01:28:46.540 --> 01:28:48.500
Well, commander, looks like you really pulled it off.

01:28:48.600 --> 01:28:51.440
Well, gentlemen, I guess we really showed them a thing or two.

01:28:51.560 --> 01:28:52.900
Doctor Adachi, we did it!

01:28:53.510 --> 01:28:54.430
Oh, yeah!

01:28:55.190 --> 01:28:56.150
Yes, sir!

01:29:06.620 --> 01:29:08.240
Oh, come on, Major.

01:29:08.580 --> 01:29:10.060
Commander, here's the colonel's son.

01:29:10.490 --> 01:29:12.170
Well, hello there, big fellow.

01:29:13.050 --> 01:29:13.390
There.

01:29:13.960 --> 01:29:14.570
Come on, now.

01:29:14.850 --> 01:29:17.700
How many saucers were there?

01:29:17.980 --> 01:29:20.040
Well, you can read all about it in the papers.

01:29:22.410 --> 01:29:23.010
Well, goodbye, Commander.

01:29:23.170 --> 01:29:24.330
Goodbye, and have a nice trip.

01:29:24.450 --> 01:29:24.870
Uh-huh.

01:29:30.480 --> 01:29:31.840
- You can terminate the alert.

01:29:31.840 --> 01:29:33.750
- Yes, sir, I will give the order.

01:29:33.750 --> 01:29:35.390
All stations, the alert is over.

01:29:35.390 --> 01:29:36.250
Conditions green.

01:29:40.730 --> 01:29:49.900
- Katsumiya, I'd like you to come along with me.

01:29:49.900 --> 01:29:51.320
I'm going to talk to the rocket pilots.

01:29:51.320 --> 01:29:52.800
- Right, sir.

01:29:52.800 --> 01:29:53.640
Let's go.

01:29:53.640 --> 01:29:54.540
- I know.

01:29:54.540 --> 01:29:55.660
- Hey, hey.

01:29:55.660 --> 01:29:56.660
- I expect to get you all.

01:29:56.660 --> 01:29:58.680
- Yes, yes, yes, yes.
